cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code, please cite the article it accompanies (preferred-citation below)."
type: software
title: "Basis-adaptive texture tomography of an Al1050 sample"
version: 2.0.0
authors:
  - family-names: "Carøe"
    given-names: "Martin Sæbye"
    affiliation: "Technical University of Denmark"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0008-3739-7562"
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/msaca-okse/basis_adaptive_textom"
abstract: >-
  Notebooks that reconstruct the orientation distribution in every voxel of a slice through an Al1050
  sample, measured by scanning 3DXRD at the DanMAX beamline (MAX IV), by texture tomography with an
  adaptive orientation basis built from point-by-point indexing of the same data.
keywords:
  - texture tomography
  - s3DXRD
  - scanning 3DXRD
  - adaptive basis
  - aluminium
  - DanMAX
  - MAX IV
